===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Any [[system]] by which [[time]] is divided into [[day]]s, [[week]]s, [[month]]s, and [[year]]s.
#: {{ux|en|The three principal '''calendars''' are the Gregorian, Jewish, and Islamic calendars.}}
# {{senseid|en|document}} A [[means]] to determine the date consisting of a [[document]] containing [[date]]s and other [[temporal]] information.
#: {{ux|en|Write his birthday on the '''calendar''' hanging on the wall.}}
# A list of planned [[event]]s.
#: {{ux|en|The club has a busy '''calendar''' this year.}}
# An orderly list or enumeration of persons, things, or events; a [[schedule]].
#: {{co|en|a '''calendar''' of bills presented in a legislative assembly;&nbsp; a '''calendar''' of causes arranged for trial in court}}
#* {{RQ:Bacon Essayes|Of Seditions and Troubles. XV.|76|''Shepherds'' of ''People'', had need know the '''''Kalenders''''' of ''Tempeſts'' in ''State''; which are commonly greateſt, when Things grow to Equality; As naturall Tempeſts are greateſt about the ''Æquinoctia''.}}
#* {{RQ:Allingham China Governess|Eye Witness|249|The story struck the depressingly familiar note with which true stories ring in the tried ears of experienced policemen.{{...}}The second note, the high alarum, not so familiar and always important since it indicates the paramount sin in Man's private '''calendar''', took most of them by surprise although they had been well prepared.}}
# {{lb|en|US}} An appointment book (US), [[appointment diary]] (UK)

